---
title: Governance before models
summary: Why sequencing policy, inventory, and evaluation ahead of model selection saves six months of rework.
publishedAt: 2026-03-12
author: KaleidoSpark
---

Most AI programmes begin with a model bake-off. The ones that finish begin with ownership.

## Start with the decision rights

Before you pick a foundation model, answer: who can approve a high-impact use case, what evidence is required, and how exceptions escalate. Without those answers, every pilot invents its own governance theatre.

## Inventory is strategy

You cannot govern what you cannot list. A lightweight inventory—system, owner, data classes, human oversight—beats a 40-page policy that nobody maps to reality.

## Evaluation is a product requirement

If you cannot describe failure modes and quality bars, you are not ready to buy or build. Evaluation harnesses are cheaper than reputational remediation.
